error[T-Bound]: `H` requires `Endpoint[(), SystemAllocator]`, and `fn(inout _incoming: RequestBody[SystemAllocator]) -> Result[Response[SystemAllocator], Error[SystemAllocator]] where carries(_incoming)` does not implement it
  --> tests/http/a_function_missing_its_request_is_not_registered.lin:11:26
   |
11 |     let routed = &router.route("GET /", greet)
   |                          ^^^^^ only the library, which declares `Endpoint[(), mem.SystemAllocator]`, may implement it for `fn(inout RequestBody[SystemAllocator]) -> Result[Response[SystemAllocator], Error[SystemAllocator]] where carries(#1)`; pass a value whose type implements it
   |
   = help: this function's parameters are `(inout)`, and `Endpoint` is implemented only for callable types whose parameters are `(read, inout)`, `(read×2..7)`, `(inout, read, inout)`, `(inout, read×2..7)` (`read×N` is N parameters taken by `read`)
